{"id" : 616, "title" : "Agent Identity Crisis: 80% of AI Agents Don't Identify Themselves, 8K MCP Servers Exposed Without Auth", "description" : "Meta Sev-1 incident in March 2026: internal AI agent skipped human approval, gave incorrect advice, exposed data for 2 hours. Agent passed every identity check but system never verified what it did after auth. DataDome tested 698K sites: 80% of agents don't identify themselves, 80% of sites don't verify. 8K MCP servers on public internet with no auth. Only 8.5% use OAuth. 30 CVEs against MCP in 60 days. 47% of CISOs observed agents with unauthorized behavior in production.", "category" : "agent_security", "github_url" : null, "github_stars" : null, "is_indexed" : true, "added_at" : "2026-05-25T21:08:17.564006+00:00"}
{"id" : 615, "title" : "DTap — DecodingTrust-Agent Platform: Full-Stack Agent Red-Teaming with 50+ Simulated Environments", "description" : "First controllable full-stack simulation platform for agent red-teaming. 50+ real-world environments (Gmail, PayPal, Slack, Robinhood, Salesforce) with full GUI/backend/MCP replicas. ~7K red-teaming tasks, 300+ risk categories from 60+ real policies. Key finding: Claude Code falls to 25%+ attacks, Google ADK loses to >50%. Deterministic judges instead of LLM-as-judge. Multi-vector attacks (environment+tool+skill+prompt). From Dawn Song lab at Berkeley. $120K API spend, 20 months development.", "category" : "agent_security", "github_url" : "https://github.com/AI-secure/DecodingTrust-Agent", "github_stars" : 38, "is_indexed" : true, "added_at" : "2026-05-25T21:07:03.660448+00:00"}
